WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:03.800
- And if you wind back the
history of our own planet

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:07.530
to almost quarter of a billion years ago.

00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:09.620
This is the map of how our world looked

00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:12.360
240 million years ago.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:14.880
Back then, if we rewind this video tape

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:17.680
of our planet's history and
the constant scudding around

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:19.370
across the surface.

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:22.430
In this period of history,
they'd all collided together

00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:26.520
and fused into a single giant landmass,

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:27.900
a super continent,

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:30.773
called Pangea, the 'All Land.'

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:36.690
And held just in the cup of
that C-shaped supercontinent

00:00:36.830 --> 00:00:39.150
was the Tethys Ocean,

00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:42.330
which over time, grew and expanded,

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:44.910
as the Atlantic is doing right now.

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:49.510
Until Pangea ripped itself
tore itself apart again,

00:00:49.510 --> 00:00:53.300
and Africa and then India rode back north

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:56.060
to re-collide, to back end
and this kind of pile up

00:00:56.060 --> 00:00:59.070
on the motorway of Earth's continents,

00:00:59.070 --> 00:01:02.530
closing up the Tethys as they went.

00:01:02.530 --> 00:01:04.530
Destroying the ancient ocean

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:06.940
swallowing it back down into the interior

00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:08.000
of the planet.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.200
This is about 15 million years ago.

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:12.030
This great ocean of Tethys now exists

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:14.940
as no more than a narrow seaway.

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:17.020
It was closed off at both ends,

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:20.293
and now exist as no more
than the puddle of Atlantic.

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:22.930
And it's that fact,

00:01:22.930 --> 00:01:25.930
the history of the Tethys in Mediterranean

00:01:25.930 --> 00:01:30.930
that explains that grand theme
through our human history.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:32.940
That because it is Africa

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:35.980
that is riding North and
colliding into Eurasia,

00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:39.270
it's crumpled up all
that northern coastline

00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:42.060
into the Alps, Carpathians,

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:42.910
the Caucasians.

00:01:42.910 --> 00:01:47.210
This is a crumpled, rippled landscape.

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:49.140
And with the rising of the sea levels

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:50.650
since the end of the last Ice Age

00:01:50.650 --> 00:01:54.770
it is now become a drowned
submerged landscape.

00:01:54.770 --> 00:01:58.480
The northern Mediterranean
is absolutely riddled

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:00.930
with natural inlets and coves

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:04.700
and bays and therefore natural harbors.

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:07.300
It is perfectly set up.

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:10.200
Perfectly conducive
for seafaring societies

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:14.680
for trading and communicating
with each other by ships.

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:16.650
Whereas the southern half Mediterranean,

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:18.590
the African coastline

00:02:18.590 --> 00:02:21.480
is flat and straight and boring.

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:23.840
It has no natural harbors.

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:26.130
Apart from Carthage here,

00:02:26.130 --> 00:02:28.350
which as you can see is
actually just on the lip

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:30.060
of effectively a subterranean mountain

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:33.330
of sub marine mountain
range linking the toe of Italy.

00:02:33.330 --> 00:02:34.680
It's about the only place

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:37.560
you can find a natural
harbor in a 1000 miles

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:40.160
of coastline around here.

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:43.860
And so it's that that
explains this great disparity

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:46.620
for thousands of years of human history.

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:49.140
It is bestowed, it's created

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:50.460
by the history of the Mediterranean

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:52.673
and these planetary forces.

